Bundled libraries

The distributed .exe is built with PyInstaller and contains these third-party
runtimes. Installing from requirements.txt fetches the same versions.

    PySide6              LGPL v3 (Qt for Python)
                         https://wiki.qt.io/Qt_for_Python
    Qt 6                 LGPL v3
                         https://www.qt.io/licensing/
    matplotlib           matplotlib licence, a BSD-style licence derived from
                         the Python Software Foundation licence
                         https://matplotlib.org/stable/users/project/license.html
    NumPy                BSD 3-Clause
                         https://numpy.org/doc/stable/license.html
    PyInstaller          GPL v2 or later, with an exception permitting the
                         bootloader to be distributed with non-GPL applications
                         https://pyinstaller.org/en/stable/license.html

PySide6 and Qt are used as unmodified shared libraries under the LGPL. The LGPL
requires that a recipient be able to replace them with a modified version; the
complete source of this application, its dependency versions and its build
script are published in this repository, which is how that is satisfied here.

Chinese text in the chart is drawn with a font already installed on the
computer, such as Microsoft YaHei on Windows. No font is bundled.

